<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Apr trade surplus widens to $6.8 bln.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Apr trade surplus widens to $6.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $6.8 billion in the first four months of this year after a $5.5 billion surplus in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS:</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE   APR 97	MAR 97	APR 96</p>
<p>    exports			    7.15	  7.35	  7.25</p>
<p>    imports			    5.75	  5.55	  6.08</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +1.40	 +1.80	 +1.17</p>
<p>Trade excluding other CIS members (trade with &quot;far abroad&quot;):</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE   APR 97	MAR 97	APR 96</p>
<p>    exports			    5.35	  5.79	  5.54</p>
<p>    imports			    4.28	  4.26	  4.33</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +1.07	 +1.53	 +1.21</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
